{
  "verso": "1.1",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "The Titanic passenger list",
    "defaultKernel": "csharp"
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "3437cebc-236d-4310-9d66-69bd316996fd",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "# The Titanic passenger list\n\nEach block below is one step of a pipeline that prepares the passenger list for a network: it reads the file beside\nthis notebook, declares the columns that take part, splits the passengers into training, validation and test rows,\nand learns everything it learns from the training rows alone. **Show the data here** on any block shows the rows as\nthey stand there, each marked with the part it lands in."
    },
    {
      "id": "91c85803-90fd-4c8c-a48a-c4a96ea49d12",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \"step\": \"read.csv\",\n  \"path\": \"data/titanic.csv\"\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "b814958d-9efb-4918-a2a3-c6b12ebf522e",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \"step\": \"declare\",\n  \"remainder\": \"drop\",\n  \"columns\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"survived\",\n      \"kind\": \"integer\",\n      \"optional\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"sibsp\",\n      \"kind\": \"integer\",\n      \"optional\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"parch\",\n      \"kind\": \"integer\",\n      \"optional\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"pclass\",\n      \"kind\": \"category\",\n      \"optional\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"sex\",\n      \"kind\": \"category\",\n      \"optional\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"age\",\n      \"kind\": \"number\",\n      \"optional\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"fare\",\n      \"kind\": \"number\",\n      \"optional\": false\n    }\n  ]\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "2f93bce4-ec04-499d-aaab-0841b5b0f2bd",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \"step\": \"split.stratified\",\n  \"column\": \"survived\",\n  \"train\": 0.7,\n  \"validation\": 0.15,\n  \"test\": 0.15,\n  \"predict\": 0,\n  \"seed\": 20260923\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "684279f6-b903-43b6-9a88-a3282a3dcba7",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \"step\": \"target\",\n  \"column\": \"survived\"\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "479a677b-101c-49c4-85c3-bc67bed7836d",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \"step\": \"fill.missing\",\n  \"column\": \"age\",\n  \"with\": \"median\"\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "84b04f81-48df-422c-bf97-84ce86c2bf80",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \"step\": \"encode.categories\",\n  \"as\": \"onehot\",\n  \"unseen\": \"reserve\"\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "00a0ce4d-4e16-4464-ada5-5f3204a5fab9",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \"step\": \"normalise\",\n  \"column\": \"age\",\n  \"scale\": \"midrange\",\n  \"outOfRange\": \"pass\"\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "67bef2ba-1304-41ce-915f-249425b736bb",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \"step\": \"normalise\",\n  \"column\": \"fare\",\n  \"scale\": \"midrange\",\n  \"outOfRange\": \"pass\"\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "380aeda8-8261-43b5-9638-717d4f1353ff",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \"step\": \"normalise\",\n  \"column\": \"sibsp\",\n  \"scale\": \"midrange\",\n  \"outOfRange\": \"pass\"\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "41c414db-0b06-4047-89dc-4f79a104a607",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \"step\": \"normalise\",\n  \"column\": \"parch\",\n  \"scale\": \"midrange\",\n  \"outOfRange\": \"pass\"\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "b3c23145-fafa-40ad-9d25-9f431d8b14f5",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \"step\": \"evidence.report\",\n  \"metrics\": [\n    \"accuracy\",\n    \"precision\",\n    \"recall\",\n    \"confusionmatrix\"\n  ],\n  \"parts\": [\n    \"validation\",\n    \"test\"\n  ],\n  \"shown\": [\n    \"numbers\",\n    \"drawn\"\n  ]\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \"step\": \"learn.network\",\n  \"layers\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"dense\",\n      \"units\": 16\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"relu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"dense\",\n      \"units\": 1\n    }\n  ],\n  \"optimizer\": {\n    \"kind\": \"adam\",\n    \"rate\": 0.01,\n    \"firstMoment\": 0.9,\n    \"secondMoment\": 0.999,\n    \"epsilon\": 1e-07\n  },\n  \"loss\": {\n    \"kind\": \"binaryCrossEntropy\"\n  },\n  \"stopping\": {\n    \"kind\": \"patience\",\n    \"patience\": 10,\n    \"least\": 0,\n    \"best\": true\n  },\n  \"engine\": \"light\",\n  \"seed\": 20260929,\n  \"epochs\": 100,\n  \"batch\": 32\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "bdd256b4-093f-4322-9fad-0478e63b1682",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "The last block names the network these rows are prepared for: its layers, what moves them, what judges them and when the run stops. The block before it names what that network is measured by. The C# cell below trains exactly the network the blocks name — it reads the pipeline they hand over, after **Show the data here** on any block or the toolbar's run, trains it, and hands back what it predicted. **Show the data here** on the report block then draws the report under its grid."
    },
    {
      "id": "19abdf82-ed61-49d8-bcd7-693783ebffc4",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "csharp",
      "source": "#r \"nuget: DeepSharp.Learners.Networks\"\n#r \"nuget: DeepSharp.Charts\"\nusing DeepSharp.Charts;\nusing DeepSharp.Learners.Networks;\nusing DeepSharp.Pipelines;\n\n// The pipeline the blocks declare, as text, run over the rows beside this notebook and trained as it says.\nvar text = Variables.Get<string>(\"deepsharp.pipeline\");\nvar folder = Variables.TryGet<string>(\"deepsharp.folder\", out var saved) ? SourceFolder.Of(saved) : SourceFolder.WorkingDirectory;\nvar declaration = PipelineDeclaration.FromJson(text, StepCatalog.BuiltIn().WithNetworks());\nvar trained = new Pipeline(declaration, rows: null, folder).Train();\n\n// What the report block measures and draws: the network's predictions, handed back as text.\nVariables.Set(\"deepsharp.predictions\", trained.Measures!.PredictionsToJson());\n\ntrained.History!.LossCurve()"
    }
  ]
}